'''PRIDE DAY!''' is [[Challenges|challenge]] #28. {{c|Isaac}} starts with {{t|Rainbow Worm}}, {{i|3 Dollar Bill}}, and {{i|Rainbow Baby}}. The goal is to defeat {{E|Mom's Heart}} or {{E|It Lives!}}. The Rainbow Worm cannot be dropped in this challenge.
__TOC__

== Difficulty ==
This is a rather casual challenge run. Many of the potential effects of the Rainbow Tears end up being beneficial overall. However, certain tears could temporarily be detrimental, such as {{i|Fire Mind}} tears causing self-damage or {{i|Proptosis}} greatly decreasing range. It is necessary to adapt to the tear trajectories given by Rainbow Worm during the run.

Although you cannot drop the Rainbow Worm, you can still acquire other trinkets through use of a Gulp! pill or any items that allow you to hold two trinkets.

== Reward ==
{{achievement text | D8 }}

== Trivia ==
* The name of the challenge "Pride Day" and the rainbow-themed items of the challenge is a reference to the LGBTQIA+ Pride community and their signature rainbow flag.
** This same signature rainbow flag appears in Mewgenics, another game by Edmund McMillen, alongside the mechanics of cats being gay, bisexual and 'Neutral' gender. When the flag was shown in a tweeted screenshot before Mewgenics released, an account asked via reply if they "would be able to disable this in the game". Edmund responded, [https://x.com/edmundmcmillen/status/1885434909680164884?lang=en in a quote tweet], "Info on your cats sexual preference is unlockable so technically yes you can disable the flag visual.. but that won’t stop the gay cats from fuckin.".

